<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nissanka Malla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1187">1187</a>–1196</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nissanka Malla was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polonnaruwa">Polonnaruwa</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a> from 1187 to 1196, a prince from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalinga">Kalinga</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. He left more inscriptions than any other Sri Lankan king, proclaiming his piety, generosity and achievements, and built monuments such as the Nissanka Lata Mandapaya. After his death the kingdom was torn by rival claimants and invasions.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nissanka-malla.jpg" alt="Nissanka Malla" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sujeewa de Silva · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Nissanka_Malla.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
